= Internet — Technical =

Internet communication is organized across administrative and protocol layers. Packet forwarding is performed across interconnected networks while end systems implement transport and application protocols. The architecture is intentionally heterogeneous: participating networks need not share internal technologies as long as they interoperate at agreed interfaces.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* Internet ≠ World Wide Web
* Internet ≠ one network operator
* Internet ≠ one application

